    "title": "datasette-llm 0.1a11",
    "summary": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a11\">datasette-llm 0.1a11</a></p> <p><code>datasette-llm</code> is the intermediate plugin for Datasette that supports configuring LLMs for use with other Datasette plugins.</p> <p>This release adds support for OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so you can configure Datasette to use an LLM hosted anywhere that talks the OpenAI pseudo-standard web protocol.</p> <p>This means that if you're running local mod",
    "body": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a11\">datasette-llm 0.1a11</a></p> <p><code>datasette-llm</code> is the intermediate plugin for Datasette that supports configuring LLMs for use with other Datasette plugins.</p> <p>This release adds support for OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so you can configure Datasette to use an LLM hosted anywhere that talks the OpenAI pseudo-standard web protocol.</p> <p>This means that if you're running local models with <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai\">LM Studio</a> or <a href=\"https://ollama.com\">Ollama</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp\">llama.cpp</a> (which just hit <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llama-cpp-v1\">v1.0.0</a>) you can run Datasette via <code>uvx</code> like thi",
