    "summary": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette-vega/releases/tag/0.7\">datasette-vega 0.7</a></p> <p>A new release of Datasette's longest untouched plugin, for rendering charts (using <a href=\"https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/\">Vega-Lite</a>) against data in a table or custom query. The last release was in July 2018!</p> <p>I finally bumped it for compatibility with the latest Datasette alphas, plus some cosmetic tweaks to make it work better with <a href=\"https://lite.",
    "body": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette-vega/releases/tag/0.7\">datasette-vega 0.7</a></p> <p>A new release of Datasette's longest untouched plugin, for rendering charts (using <a href=\"https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/\">Vega-Lite</a>) against data in a table or custom query. The last release was in July 2018!</p> <p>I finally bumped it for compatibility with the latest Datasette alphas, plus some cosmetic tweaks to make it work better with <a href=\"https://lite.datasette.io/\">Datasette Lite</a>.</p> <p>(Datasette Lite just gained the ability to run JavaScript plugins like this! I'll write more about that soon.)</p> <p>Since it works with Datasette Lite, the live demo in the README now <a href=\"https://lite.datasette.io/?install=datasette-vega&amp;csv=https",
    "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/14/datasette-vega/",
